  "role": "fossil record of the extinct rugose and heterocoral taxa Thompson discusses (Heterophyllia, Zaphrentis, Cyathophyllidae, Rugosa/Tetracoralla, Streptelasma) and deep-time context for the extant lineages",
  "notes": "PBDB spells the genus 'Zaphrentis Haime 1850' and treats it as a subjective synonym of Zaphrenthis; Heterophyllia angulata is credited to Duncan 1868 (GBIF: 1867). Not covered: Nereis, Pyrosoma, Leucothea (404 not found); Echinus (PBDB resolves the name to the class Echinoidea by rank change, so no genus-level count exists); Alcyonium (PBDB's 'Alcyonium Hisinger 1823' is an unclassified homonym with 0 occurrences); Pelophylax esculentus and Styela canopus (not queried; no fossil record expected).",
